 3
Create a Procedure that displays all Procedure and Function
names from the current schema by querying USER_SOURCE table
using an Explicit Cursor.
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;

sql> CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE LIST_OBJECTS
IS

CURSOR C1 IS
SELECT DISTINCT NAME,TYPE
FROM USER_SOURCE
WHERE TYPE IN ('PROCEDURE','FUNCTION')
ORDER BY TYPE,NAME;

V_NAME USER_SOURCE.NAME%TYPE;
V_TYPE USER_SOURCE.TYPE%TYPE;

BEGIN

OPEN C1;

LOOP

FETCH C1 INTO V_NAME,V_TYPE;

EXIT WHEN C1%NOTFOUND;

DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(V_TYPE||' : '||V_NAME);

END LOOP;

CLOSE C1;

END;
/

Output:
-------

Procedure created.


Execute:
--------

sql> EXEC LIST_OBJECTS;

Output:
-------

FUNCTION : ADD_NUM
PROCEDURE : EMP_DETAILS
PROCEDURE : LIST_OBJECTS

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.

